Specifically, if the array contains a 0, the original product is 0.
If we add 1 to a 0, it becomes 1. The product becomes the product of the other digits.
If we add 1 to a non-zero digit, the product remains 0 (because the 0 is still there).
So if there is at least one 0, we should consider adding 1 to that 0 to potentially get a non-zero product. If there are multiple 0s, adding 1 to one of them makes it 1, but the other 0s remain 0, so the product is still 0.
